      },
      "description": "How long until each PE infrastructure filesystem reaches zero bytes free, at the rate it is filling over the last forecast window. **Empty is the healthy state**: the series only exists while a filesystem is actually losing space, so nothing to draw means nothing is heading for the wall. tmpfs and overlay mounts are excluded, because a full tmpfs is a symptom rather than a volume anybody sizes. PdctngFilesystemFillingSoon pages when a line falls under the configured threshold.",
